#
# An index: an aggregator named like a manifest discovery finds, with no
# mf:entries of its own and a member named like a discovered manifest at or
# below its own directory. Discovery finds it beside `group/manifest.ttl`; the
# runner runs the group as its own case and checks the index for coverage,
# never running the group through it, so no case runs twice. Its neighbours
# `index-with-entries/`, `index-undiscovered-member/` and
# `index-outside-member/` break one condition each and are refused.
@prefix mf: <http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/DataAccess/tests/test-manifest#> .

<> a mf:Manifest ;
    mf:include ( <group/manifest.ttl> ) .
